/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.swp
.idea/

# Design records and point-in-time assessments, written for whoever is working
# on the engine. They are working notes rather than documentation, they argue
# with themselves as the work lands, and they are nobody's business but this
# machine's — so they stay out of the repository entirely rather than out of the
# published crate.
/audit/

# The fuzzing harnesses are tracked; everything the fuzzer produces is not.
# A corpus and a crash file are machine-local artifacts of one run, and a corpus
# checked in goes stale the moment a parser's framing changes.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
/fuzz/Cargo.lock
